rECC0ToGIPbwjvisz1r4O0G2BxgB"},{"$type":"text","text":"This page shows how to run louis-agent with Docker, first on your own machine and then in Azure. It has three parts:\n\n- **On your own machine:** two Docker stacks. One runs the coding agent\u0027s API and its code-review app on port 5082. The other runs louis-agent.dev on port 5080 and this site on port 5084.\n- **Watch every turn:** an Aspire dashboard on port 18888. It shows each turn, model request and tool call as a trace. It keeps everything in memory, so a restart clears it.\n- **Shipped in Azure:** every merge to main releases both sites through \u0060deploy-sites.yml\u0060. Each site is an Azure Container App that sleeps when nobody visits, so the first visitor after a quiet spell waits a few seconds."},{"$type":"functionCall","name":"Offer","arguments":{"question":"Where would you like to go next?","choices":[{"label":"Walk me through this page","why":"One section at a time, in the page\u0027s order.","suggested":true},{"label":"Explain the two stacks","why":"What each Docker stack runs and which ports it uses."},{"label":"How the sites reach Azure","why":"What happens on a merge, and what deploy.ps1 does."}]},"informationalOnly":false,"callId":"toolu_01CCB5qZzTb6q8iubeKEGYiv"}],"messageId":"msg_011ChSS19Gf5CaVuiyqJeNbv"}],"responseId":"msg_011ChSS19Gf5CaVuiyqJeNbv","modelId":"claude-haiku-5-5","createdAt":"2026-11-26T23:47:04.5901003\u002B00:00","finishReason":"tool_calls","usage":{"inputTokenCount":10118,"outputTokenCount":1049,"totalTokenCount":11167,"cachedInputTokenCount":9217,"additionalCounts":{"CacheCreationInputTokens":897}}}